# vtium-clipboard and its short name vticlip, which copy text from a
# script or a pipe to the console's clipboard (ADR-1007). The program
# writes OSC 52 to its own terminal, then asks XTVERSION and DA1, and its
# exit status says whether vtium answered. Tier 1 judges the bytes
# (tools/conformance/scenarios/vtium-clipboard-copy.scenario). This guide
# checks what a person sees: the copy pastes back with Shift+Insert and the
# middle mouse button, and each refusal says why.
#
# The first step builds the program with cargo and links it as vticlip in
# /tmp/vtium-vt/bin, so every step names that directory. make vt-check runs
# the guide from the checkout's top directory, where cargo finds the
# workspace. Each step that pastes reads one line with the shell's read, so
# the pasted text shows on the screen with what the step expects.
#
#   make vt-check GUIDE=clipboard

title: copy text to the console's clipboard with vticlip

intro: vticlip copy reads text from a file or from a pipe and copies it to
intro: the console's clipboard. Shift+Insert and the middle mouse button
intro: paste it. Each step runs the commands for you, then shows the
intro: program's exit status: 0 means vtium took the copy, and any other
intro: number means it did not.

step: Build vticlip
run: cargo build -q --release -p vtium-clipboard && mkdir -p /tmp/vtium-vt/bin && ln -sfn "$(pwd)/${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/release/vtium-clipboard" /tmp/vtium-vt/bin/vticlip && /tmp/vtium-vt/bin/vticlip --version; sleep 3
expect: cargo builds the program, which can take a minute. The last line
expect: reads *vticlip* and a version number.

step: Copy from a pipe, then paste with Shift+Insert
run: clear; echo hello | /tmp/vtium-vt/bin/vticlip copy; echo "exit status $?"; printf 'Press Shift+Insert, then Enter: '; read -r line; printf 'You pasted: %s\n' "$line"; sleep 5
expect: The first line reads *exit status 0*, with no message above it.
expect: Shift+Insert types *hello* after the prompt, and the last line
expect: reads "You pasted: hello".

step: Copy a file with accents, wide characters and emoji, then paste with the middle button
run: clear; printf 'café 中文 😀\n' > /tmp/vtium-vt/clip.txt; /tmp/vtium-vt/bin/vticlip copy /tmp/vtium-vt/clip.txt; echo "exit status $?"; printf 'Press the middle mouse button, then Enter: '; read -r line; printf 'You pasted: %s\n' "$line"; sleep 5
expect: The first line reads *exit status 0*. The middle button pastes
expect: *café 中文 😀* after the prompt, each character whole, and the last
expect: line shows the same text.

step: Copy with the output redirected
run: clear; echo redirected | /tmp/vtium-vt/bin/vticlip copy > /tmp/vtium-vt/clip-out.txt; echo "exit status $?, $(wc -c < /tmp/vtium-vt/clip-out.txt) bytes in the output file"; printf 'Press Shift+Insert, then Enter: '; read -r line; printf 'You pasted: %s\n' "$line"; sleep 5
expect: The first line reads *exit status 0, 0 bytes in the output file*:
expect: the copy went to the console, not to the file. Shift+Insert pastes
expect: *redirected*.

step: Text too large for the clipboard
run: clear; head -c 600000 /dev/zero | tr '\0' a | /tmp/vtium-vt/bin/vticlip copy; echo "exit status $?"; printf 'Press Shift+Insert, then Enter: '; read -r line; printf 'You pasted: %s\n' "$line"; sleep 5
expect: A message says the text is more than 524288 bytes and that
expect: *nothing was copied*, and the next line reads exit status 1.
expect: Shift+Insert still pastes *redirected*, the text of the step before.

step: Text that is not valid UTF-8
run: clear; printf 'h\377i' | /tmp/vtium-vt/bin/vticlip copy; echo "exit status $?"; printf 'Press Shift+Insert, then Enter: '; read -r line; printf 'You pasted: %s\n' "$line"; sleep 5
expect: A message says the text is not all valid UTF-8, and the next line
expect: reads exit status 0. Shift+Insert pastes h, then
expect: *the replacement character*, a question mark in a diamond or a box,
expect: then i.

step: Paste from a program is not available
run: clear; /tmp/vtium-vt/bin/vticlip paste; echo "exit status $?"; sleep 8
expect: A message starting with "vticlip:" says that
expect: *paste is not available yet*, and points to Shift+Insert and the
expect: middle mouse button. The next line reads exit status 2.
